title: 'sp-api: Use EncodeLike for runtime API client-side parameters'

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Runtime API client-side methods generated by `decl_runtime_apis!` now accept any argument
    that produces the same SCALE encoding as the declared parameter type, instead of requiring
    the exact type. This reuses the existing `EncodeLike<T>` trait from `parity-scale-codec`:
    each method parameter becomes generic over `EncodeLike<DeclaredType>`, so both the value and a
    reference to it (as well as other `EncodeLike` types such as `Box<T>` or `Cow<T>`) can be
    passed. Because the parameters are forwarded via SCALE anyway, this adds no runtime cost and
    simplifies node-side code that previously had to construct the exact parameter type.

    To keep the generated traits dyn-compatible, parameterised methods now carry a
    `where Self: Sized` bound. `mock_impl_runtime_apis!` keeps working with concrete types by
    decoding the generic parameters back into the declared types inside the generated method
    bodies.

    Because `EncodeLike<T>` (unlike a blanket `Encode`-based trait) is not implemented for every
    encodable type by default, the core block component traits that are used as runtime API
    parameters now require the `EncodeLike` marker: `sp_runtime::traits::Header`,
    `Block::Extrinsic` and `sp_consensus_beefy::AuthorityIdBound`. Every type deriving `Encode`
    already satisfies this, so no implementor changes are required.
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Some node-side call sites that relied on type inference (e.g. passing `block.into()`, a bare
    `vec![]` or `None`) now need the concrete type to be spelled out, because `EncodeLike` has
    more blanket implementations than the previous approach and can make inference ambiguous. In
    particular, a `Block` value can now be passed directly to `Core::execute_block` /
    `BlockBuilder::check_inherents` (it already `EncodeLike`s its `LazyBlock`), so the explicit
    `.into()` conversions to `LazyBlock` are no longer needed.

crates:
- name: sp-api
  bump: major
- name: sp-api-proc-macro
  bump: patch
- name: sp-runtime
  bump: major
- name: sp-consensus-beefy
  bump: major
